{
  "_note": "Every sound in the game, made by the page's synth (web/audio.js) from these recipes; there are no audio files. Read and checked by crates/core/src/sound/. A cue plays once; a loop plays while the game names it, at the gain and pitch the game sets each frame. Frequencies in Hz, times in ms, gains 0 to 1 (the layers of one cue add up, so keep their sum under about 1), filter Q as WebAudio's, wobble depth in cents. Hear each one on the Sounds screen (Gallery, Sounds).",
  "_layers": "A cue layer: wave (sine, square, sawtooth, triangle or noise), freq and an optional to_freq it glides to over the layer (glide exp or linear), at_ms (when it starts), attack_ms, hold_ms, release_ms, gain, an optional filter {type lowpass/highpass/bandpass, freq, to_freq, q}, an optional wobble {rate, cents}, stretch (hold as long as the game asks), notes [[at_ms, freq], ...] (one copy per note: a tune, or a chord when the times match) and repeat {times, every_ms}. Noise has no freq; colour it with a filter.",
  "_events": "Game events (crates/core/src/sim MatchEvent, by name) to cues. who: all, mine (the listener's own seat) or others. {field} puts in an event field; each lists the values it can take. How to add one: the top of crates/core/src/sound/events.rs.",
  "noise": { "samples": 32768, "seed": 7 },
  "smooth_ms": 60,
  "fade_ms": 250,
  "max_pending": 32,
